    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0494" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg424"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr. Mercier.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 12, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to the letter from a Frenchman at
                    New York to the consul general of France there, relating to wines being
                    considered by the custom-house authorities at that place as contraband of war,
                    which you some days since left at this department, I now have the honor to
                    enclose to you, for your information, the copy of a communication of the 6th
                    instant from the Secretary of the Treasury, to whom the matter was referred,
                    from which it appears that wines, as they do not properly come under the head of
                    ardent spirits, are permitted to be shipped.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Mercier</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d368-a1.xml" xpointer="d368-a1"/>
            </div>
